<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fehrbellin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1675">1675</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scanian-war">Scanian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fehrbellin was fought on 28 June 1675 near the town of Fehrbellin, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-elector-of-brandenburg">Frederick William, the Great Elector</a>, and a Swedish army that had invaded the electorate. Brandenburg's cavalry, led in the attack by Frederick of Hesse-Homburg, defeated the Swedes. The victory ended the reputation of Swedish invincibility and raised the standing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg-prussia">Brandenburg-Prussia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fehrbellin.jpg" alt="Battle of Fehrbellin" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dismar Degen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_bei_Fehrbellin2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
